When a provider returns 401, yoyo's hint now says where the key actually came from. Before, it said "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set" to someone who had passed --api-key. Committed as 9eff971c (Part of #1062). fmt, clippy with -D warnings, build and the full cargo test all pass.

The cause: the 401 branch decided "set" or "not set" by checking whether the provider's own environment variable existed. That check misses a key given with --api-key, a key from the config file, an alternate name like GEMINI_API_KEY, and the fallback to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or API_KEY.

What changed:
• Recording the source: src/cli.rs now records where the key came from while it looks the key up. The variable name comes from the same lookup function the #1064 work added, so there is no second list of names.
• The wording: a new helper, auth_failure_message, in src/prompt_retry.rs builds the hint from that recorded source. Its tests are in a new file, src/prompt_retry_auth_tests.rs, and compare full strings. When no key was found, or the key came from the provider's own variable, the text is exactly what it was before.

Before and after, checked live against a local server that always answers 401, with a clean environment:

| Key came from | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| --api-key | OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. plus an export line | names --api-key as the rejected key; no export line |
| ANTHROPIC_API_KEY only | OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. | says the Anthropic key was sent instead |
| api_key in .yoyo.toml | OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. | names the config file |
| google with GEMINI_API_KEY | GOOGLE_API_KEY is not set. | names GEMINI_API_KEY |
| OPENAI_API_KEY | | unchanged |

One gap in the tests: the code that records the source is switched off under cfg!(test). Otherwise the in-process tests of argument parsing would set the shared value first and break the older tests that read the environment. So no unit test covers the recording step; only the live run above checks it.

Beyond the three planned files:
• Size limits: tests/module_size.rs raises the recorded sizes of src/cli.rs (7685 → 7769; +17 are mine, the other +67 were already over) and src/prompt_retry.rs (2720 → 2785). Both were warnings rather than failures; raising the recorded size is the check's own suggested fix.
• ARCHITECTURE.md: a short note on the prompt_retry.rs entry.
• Docs: none of the pages in docs/src or the README quoted the old wording, so they needed no change.

I commented on #1062 with the before/after table. The ticket stays open: --api-key still doesn't stop the first-run setup wizard (setup::needs_setup_from takes no command-line input, main.rs:1033), and that is what the issue's title is about.
